Rāma burns with grief over stolen Sītā --- Rāma eyes strung bow sighing to destroy worlds --- Lakṣmaṇa pleads with folded hands --- Lakṣmaṇa marks lone broken chariot and blood --- Lakṣmaṇa calls Rāma refuge of beings --- Lakṣmaṇa urges search with sages' aid --- Lakṣmaṇa counsels conciliation first then arrows